    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6347" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calvĭtĭum</span></b> , ii,
			n.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>baldness</i> (class.; access. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calvĭtĭes</span></b> ).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: in luctu capillum sibi evellere, quasi
			calvitio maeror levaretur, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc.
				3, 26, 62</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 11, 37, 47, § 131</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Dom. 18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aus. Epigr. 72, 2</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Nat. 1, 10 <i>fin.</i></span></i> —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Of places destitute of herbage, <i>bareness</i>, <i>sterility</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 4,
				29, 11</span></i>.</div>
